# Melanoma Classification using Deep Learning

## Objective

Binary classification of dermoscopic skin lesion images to predict
whether a lesion is malignant.

## Dataset

SIIM-ISIC Melanoma Classification dataset.

The dataset contains:
- Training metadata
- Test metadata
- JPEG images
- DICOM images
- TFRecord files

## Approach

1. Load metadata from train.csv and test.csv
2. Construct image paths
3. Split training data into training and validation sets
4. Apply image transformations
5. Train an EfficientNet-based binary classifier
6. Evaluate using ROC-AUC
7. Generate probability predictions for test images
8. Create submission.csv

## Model

EfficientNet-based binary classifier with a single output neuron.

Loss:
BCEWithLogitsLoss

Optimizer:
[PUT YOUR ACTUAL OPTIMIZER HERE]

Evaluation metric:
ROC-AUC

## Preliminary Results

Training samples: 5760
Validation samples: 4903
Epochs: 1

Training AUC: 0.9316
Validation AUC: 0.8586

Test predictions generated: 5180

## Repository Structure

notebooks/  - training notebook
src/        - dataset, model, training and inference code
results/    - experimental results
report/     - report figures

## Note

The reported experiment uses a reduced training subset and one epoch
due to computational constraints. Results should therefore be
interpreted as a preliminary experiment rather than the final
fully-trained model performance.
